"""Grade 12, Days 161-170 -- extends Grade 12 from 160 to 170 days. Topics
chosen after dumping the full existing Day 1-160 title list (data/grade12.json,
640 subject entries) to avoid any overlap -- Grade 12 has been extremely
heavily mined across sixteen prior batches, so this batch hunts for angles
not yet touched: the morality play, the revenge tragedy, Menippean satire,
the closet drama, ergodic literature and hypertext fiction, erasure poetry,
the jeremiad, the verse essay, and the roman-fleuve for English; the
Student t-distribution, analysis of variance (ANOVA), Hamiltonian paths and
cycles, Dijkstras algorithm, the stable marriage problem, Fermat primes and
constructible polygons, Bertrands postulate, Liouville numbers, and the
Runge phenomenon for Advanced Functions; systems of linear differential
equations, Sturm-Liouville theory, the Adams-Bashforth multistep method,
Monte Carlo integration, the Gibbs phenomenon, Cesaro summation, the
Riemann rearrangement theorem, asymptotic expansions, and the total
derivative for Calculus; gyroscopic precession, rolling without slipping,
the Poynting vector, LC circuits, polarization and Malus law, the quantum
harmonic oscillator, exoplanet detection, Olbers paradox, and band theory
of solids for Physics. Every one of these 36 titles/key terms was checked
against the full Day 1-160 dump and confirmed absent. Day 170 is a review
day, following the exact per-subject review pattern used on Day 150/160:
one review lesson per subject, each quizzing the first five of that
subject's nine new topics.

Subject keys for Grade 12 are "English", "AdvancedFunctions", "Calculus",
"Physics" (same as all earlier Grade 12 batches).

videoUrl is intentionally left unset for every subject -- fetch_video_ids.py
fills these in automatically on its next daily run. No embedded ASCII
double-quote or straight-apostrophe characters are used anywhere in
title/question/summary/option text; apostrophes and accented characters
are avoided entirely, matching the convention used since the Days 131-140
batch and followed exactly by the Days 151-160 batch immediately before
this one.
"""
